---
name: sprint-group
version: 4.4.0
description: Beads formula for the dev, sanity and QA tasks of one sprint, attached under its sprint container. bead-groups supplies every variable.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - parent
  - ref
  - phase
  - sprint
  - stack
  - layer
  - difficulty
  - branch
  - worktree
  - pr_target
  - priority
  - edge_option
  - stack_bead
  - checked_title
  - phase_feature
  - lint_command
  - policy_path
  - max_sanity_rounds
  - reviewers_round1
  - children
---
{#
sc-compose beads formula (sc-compose/beads/v1, ADR-0021): the dev, sanity and
QA tasks of one sprint, poured directly under its existing sprint container.
Poured ids are <parent>.<ref>-<step> (see bead_formulas.attach_id).

`{{{ ... }}}` are compose variables, baked at render time; sc-compose escapes
them for TOML strings. This formula declares no bead variables, so every
value here is a compose variable;
this comment names no double-brace example because sc-compose --strict reads
tokens inside comments (sc-compose#785). layer and priority
are written bare and must be integers.

Compose variables (bead-groups fills them from the sprint container, the
repository configuration and sprint-group.relations.json):
  parent         the sprint container id
  ref            attach reference, "group"
  phase, sprint, stack, layer, difficulty, priority
  stack_bead, checked_title, phase_feature, lint_command, policy_path,
  max_sanity_rounds
                 the close fields (close_fields.POURED) every step carries, so
                 its close reads no other bead; max_sanity_rounds is bare
  reviewers_round1  the QA step's reviewer list, from the repository configuration
  children       the sprint's stage:subtask numbers ("1" for <parent>.sub-1), from bd children;
                 [] when the sprint has none. Each pours a sub-<n>-sanity step; the
                 sprint's own sanity step needs them all
  edge_option    E1: "C" sanity needs dev (poured `blocks`; the default),
                 "B" no sanity -> dev edge in the pour (bead-groups adds
                 `validates`), "A" only dev is poured
The sanity step carries metadata.dev_bead (N9: it signals that the sanity
agent runs on this sprint) and difficulty.

No step sets an assignee: every poured bead carries `difficulty` and the lead
picks the agent at dispatch (`bd update <bead> --assignee <agent>`).

Closers: the dev closes dev; dev-sanity closes sanity on PASS only, and on
FAIL reopens dev and leaves sanity open, which re-blocks it through
`needs dev`; quality-mgr closes qa after pouring a finding-group for each
blocking finding and filing the important and minor ones; the team lead
closes the sprint container, which bd refuses while any group bead under it
is open.
#}
formula = "sprint-group"
description = "Sprint {{{ sprint }}}: dev, sanity and QA under sprint container {{{ parent }}}."
version = 4
type = "workflow"

[[steps]]
id = "dev"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: dev"
description = "Dev work for sprint {{{ sprint }}}. The deliverables and acceptance criteria are on the sprint container {{{ parent }}}."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:dev"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
layer = {{{ layer }}}
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
{% if edge_option != "A" %}

[[steps]]
id = "sanity"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: sanity check"
description = "Sanity check of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev (sprint {{{ sprint }}}): each numbered deliverable is written and lint passes. This is not QA. Close on PASS only; on FAIL reopen the dev bead and leave this bead open."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:dev-sanity"]
{% if edge_option == "C" or children %}needs = [{% if edge_option == "C" %}"dev"{% if children %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% for n in children %}"sub-{{{ n }}}-sanity"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}]
{% endif %}
[steps.metadata]
role = "sanity"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
dev_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev"
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"

{% for n in children %}
[[steps]]
id = "sub-{{{ n }}}-sanity"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: sub-{{{ n }}} sanity check"
description = "Sanity check of subtask {{{ parent }}}.sub-{{{ n }}} of sprint {{{ sprint }}}: each of its numbered deliverables is written. Close on PASS only. The sprint's dev task is {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:dev-sanity"]
{% if edge_option == "C" %}needs = ["dev"]
{% endif %}
[steps.metadata]
role = "sanity"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.sub-{{{ n }}}"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sub-{{{ n }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
dev_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev"
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
{% endfor %}
[[steps]]
id = "qa"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: QA round 1"
description = "QA round 1 of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev (sprint {{{ sprint }}}), after its sanity check passes."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:qa"]
needs = ["sanity"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "qa"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
round = 1
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-dev"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
reviewers_round1 = [{% for r in reviewers_round1 %}"{{{ r }}}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}]
{% endif %}
